<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Denis of Portugal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1261–1325</span> · Also known as Dinis of Portugal, Denis the Farmer King</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Denis (Dinis) was king of Portugal from 1279 to 1325. He fixed the border with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-alcanices">Treaty of Alcañices</a> in 1297, founded the university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> in 1290, made Portuguese the language of government and founded the Order of Christ in 1319 to take over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Templars</a>' property. Known as the Farmer King, he encouraged agriculture and planted the pine forest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leiria">Leiria</a>, and was himself a noted poet.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/denis-of-portugal.jpg" alt="Denis of Portugal" width="320" height="509" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:D._Dinis_-_Compendio_de_cr%C3%B3nicas_de_reyes_(Biblioteca_Nacional_de_Espa%C3%B1a).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
